{"availability":"available","full":"alperdincer/pyodide_drought_calculator","name":"pyodide_drought_calculator","description":"Drought Indicator (SPI) Calculator with Pyodide on Web","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-10-05T14:58:06Z","updated":"2025-10-05T15:14:59Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://drought-calculator.pages.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:22.967Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:22.967Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:22.967Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T17:59:36.740Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:13:26.724Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:22.967Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser-based Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI) calculator built using WebAssembly (WASM) and Pyodide, allowing Python-based drought analysis to run entirely client-side — no server, no installation, no dependencies.","The SPI Modular App brings climate analytics directly to the browser. It uses Pyodide (Python compiled to WebAssembly) to execute scientific computations like SPI, traditionally performed with the climate-indices library, right inside a web page.","This project demonstrates how WASM + Python can power next-generation climate-tech tools — fast, private, and accessible from anywhere."],"features":["🐍 Python in the Browser — via Pyodide","⚙️ Modular Architecture — JavaScript modules handle data, computation, and visualization","🌦️ Drought Indices — Calculate SPI-1, SPI-3, SPI-6, SPI-12, SPI-24","📊 Interactive UI — Editable tables for precipitation data entry","📈 Instant Results — SPI values, drought categories, and statistics"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alperdincer/pyodide_drought_calculator/blob/main/readme.md","fingerprint":"62d52316e43b6c59600fbaf7f5c492e01a855b5cfe9b734737e3d017cfbe53d0","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T17:59:37.076Z"},"overviewChecke